  "applies_to": "Eastron SDM120CT-40mA single-phase CT-connected DIN-rail meter with RS485 Modbus RTU, user manual V1.0 (2026-07-16).",
  "summary": "The SDM120CT-40mA is a single-phase two-wire DIN-rail meter that measures through external current transformers and reports over RS485 Modbus RTU. Readings are IEEE floats in input registers (function 04) covering voltage, current, powers, power factor, frequency, demand and import/export energy. Holding registers (function 03/16) hold the RS485 settings, CT primary, pulse outputs and demand period.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Tables print Modicon numbers (30001, 40003, six-digit 461457...) beside the hex start address used on the wire. Wire address = printed number minus 30001 / 40001 / 400001; the manual's example reads 30001 at start address 0x0000."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "SDM120CT-40mA user manual",
    "doc_number": "V1.0",
    "revision_date": "2026-07-16",
    "url": "https://www.eastrongroup.com/eastrongroup/2026/07/17/EastronSDM120CT-M40mAUsermanualV10.pdf",
    "pages": "Chapter 4, PDF pages 17-23"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the manual states floats are sent big-endian with the high 16 bits in the first register, and its example decodes 43 66 00 00 as 230 V. All floats here are ABCD.",
    "Left out: metering mode (printed 463779 but with hex start address F9 20, which corresponds to 463777). The printed number and the hex address disagree, so the register is omitted until confirmed.",
    "Left out: scroll display time (463745), stored as BCD, which this schema cannot represent.",
    "Left out: serial number (464513), an unsigned 32-bit value with no stated word order.",
    "This map is for the SDM120CT-40mA only. The SDM120-M (direct connect) user manual on eastrongroup.com has no register table, so it is not covered here.",
    "The front-panel CT1 menu offers fixed primaries (5 to 600 A) while register 40051 accepts 5 to 9999; values outside the menu list have not been checked on a meter."
  ],
